WEBVTT

00:02:29.005 --> 00:02:30.391
to answer questions,

00:02:30.415 --> 00:02:31.732
to construct models

00:02:31.756 --> 00:02:33.275
and to develop hypotheses.

00:02:33.692 --> 00:02:36.965
Students then go to the virtual world
to test their hypotheses

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:38.455
and see if they're accurate,

00:02:38.479 --> 00:02:40.629
much as scientists go to the field

00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:42.323
in their careers.

00:02:43.054 --> 00:02:45.215
When students return
to their digital journal,

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:47.573
they share their observations, claims,

00:02:47.597 --> 00:02:49.393
reasoning and evidence.

00:02:49.925 --> 00:02:54.086
The students' written answers
and virtual interactions

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.864
are all updated live

00:02:55.888 --> 00:02:57.865
in an educator assessment dashboard,

00:02:57.889 --> 00:03:00.402
so that teachers can follow their progress